# Content-Security-Policy, tightened 2026-09-12. It used to read
# `default-src 'self' https:` with `connect-src 'self' https:` and
# `frame-src 'self' https:`, which allowed the page to talk to, and embed,
# any host on the internet — so it documented nothing and stopped nothing.
# Every origin below is one the client code actually reaches; the inventory
# behind it is in CLAUDE.md under "What the CSP allows, and why".
#
# Two wildcards are deliberate and should stay:
#   img-src https:  — the Comic widget renders images straight from whatever
#                     webcomic host a feed names, so the set is unknowable.
#                     Images can't execute, so this is the cheap wildcard.
#   'unsafe-inline' — the GA4 tag must stay inline in <head> on every page
#                     (Google's detector scans served HTML), and JS sets
#                     inline styles throughout. A nonce can't come from a
#                     static _headers file; it would need the Worker to
#                     rewrite every HTML response.
#
# https://happening-now.net is listed in connect-src even though it IS 'self'
# in production. That is for previews: a staged build served from 127.0.0.1
# still calls the production Worker for /v1 data (see API_ORIGIN in
# assets/common.js), which is cross-origin there and same-origin here. Without
# it a local preview reports violations production would never see.
#
# Adding a third-party endpoint means adding it here too, or it works locally
# (python -m http.server sends no CSP) and is blocked in production only.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://happening-now.net https://cloudflareinsights.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://api.open-meteo.com https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com https://api.weather.gov https://api.zippopotam.us https://api.bigdatacloud.net https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org; frame-src 'self' https://embed.windy.com; media-src 'self' blob:; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; form-action 'self' https://duckduckgo.com; upgrade-insecure-requests

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Static assets: cache for 1h, then revalidate via ETag. Service worker
# (network-first) still gets fresh content within 1h via its own logic;
# new deploys take effect immediately because HTML is uncached and the
# referenced asset URLs hit Cloudflare's CDN, which is purged on deploy.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate
